.\" Manual page for Zervo. Deliberately short: the browser has one argument.
.TH ZERVO 1 "2026-08-22" "Zervo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zervo \- a sidebar-first browser built on the Servo engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zervo
.RI [ URL ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Zervo
is a browser chrome \(em sidebar, workspaces, tabs, settings \(em wrapped around
Servo, the independent web engine written in Rust. There is no Chromium and no
Gecko underneath.
.PP
Servo is not yet a complete web engine, so some sites will not work. This is an
experiment rather than a browser to depend on.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I URL
Open this address instead of the configured homepage. A bare word that is not a
URL is put through the configured search engine. An address beginning
.B zervo://
names one of Zervo's own pages and is opened over the homepage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SERVO_STYLE_THREAD_STACK_SIZE_KB
Size, in kilobytes, of the stack given to each style thread. Unoptimised Stylo
frames overflow the engine's 512\ KB default on complex pages.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter, in the usual
.BR env_logger (3)
syntax.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/Zervo/
Settings, history, bookmarks and the password index.
.SH BUGS
Report problems at
.UR https://github.com/Goddv/Zervo/issues
.UE .
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://servo.org
The Servo engine
.UE .
